dialect protocol
protocol stdio.bmp.diff
version 1
schema stdio.bmp.diff
start diff

# P2-FG2: `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` for `BmpDiff` are derive-generated
# (`#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]`, ../🦀️.rs) via `🗣️dsl/✨️derive/🦀️.rs`'s `DslDiff`
# region -- ALREADY real binary, NOT the F6-era `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut this file used to (wrongly) document as a bare JSON payload (confirmed by direct
# reading: `encode_diff` calls `store::pack_rt::encode_document`, never `print_diff`/serde_json).
# Same framework-generic `.spk` document container every `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` type in the
# repo routes through (this ticket's own recipe §2.4/§5 `txt-diffcodec-spk-container-is-
# framework-level`) -- copied verbatim in shape from `stdio.txt`'s own already-real diff protocol
# (`🔤️txt/…/🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio`), the first pilot to land this exact
# pattern; only `protocol`/`schema` above differ.
#
# `encode_document` wraps the record in the FULL `.spk` document container
# (`🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️.rs`, `MAGIC = [0x89,'S','P','K',0x0D,0x0A,0x1A,0x0A]`) -- a real,
# checksummed, chunk-table-indexed, optionally-deflate-compressed random-access file format, not
# a lightweight per-message frame. This file models the one fixed, ALWAYS-present, self-
# contained structure: the 32-byte superblock header (`Header::write_bytes`/`Header::parse`) --
# magic, format version, feature-flag bitfields, and a self-CRC over the first 20 bytes (the CRC
# value itself is opaque here -- this dialect has no CRC-verification primitive, same
# "structurally irreducible" treatment M2 already gives every other checksum). Every OTHER byte
# of a real `.spk` file (segment table, chunk table, symbol table, the deflate-compressed record
# body itself, and an 84-byte FOOTER magic-scanned backward from EOF) forms a real random-access,
# checksum-validated, compressed document container -- the SAME category of complexity the
# user's own decisions and M2's own scope already carve out for DWG's compression pipeline and
# PDF/1.7's full indirect-object graph: an imperative, checksum/compression-driven transform, not
# a declarative fixed layout. `.spk` is furthermore a FRAMEWORK-level container -- shared
# verbatim by every `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` type in the whole repo, not anything specific to
# `stdio.bmp` -- so a full per-segment/footer description belongs at a framework-level
# `pack_format.protocol.semio` file (mirroring M3's own `semio.envelope` precedent), out of this
# per-artifact ticket's ownership boundary (recorded in this wave's own `mechanism_gaps`).
# Modeled honestly: the 32-byte header IS genuinely, individually byte-walked and validated,
# field for field; everything past it is one opaque tail.
framing magic 0x8953504B0D0A1A0A
header fixed 24
field version_major u16
field version_minor u16
field required_flags u32
field optional_flags u32
field header_crc32 u32
field reserved fixed 8
chain bytes
